<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40442" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rāsūra</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a scraping</i>, <i>a shaving</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calami,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 29, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">barbae capitisque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. in Isa. 5, 15, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Concr., <i>what is scraped</i> or <i>shaved off; a scraping</i>, <i>shaving</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eboris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. 1, 10, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6</span></i> (4), 8, 8.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gulae,</span>”
				<i>the harsh pronunciation of the gutturals by the
						Orientals</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. in Ep. Paul. ad Tit. 2, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
